        "original_id": "62146e91-ddd6-5cbf-84e5-5cd30496fea1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rosario Dawson, Rachael Leigh Cook, Abrima Erwiah\n- Films and TV: Josie and the Pussycats, Kids, She's All That, Into the West, Perception, Robot Chicken\n- Organizations and Projects: Studio One Eighty Nine, Fashion Rising, V-Day Movement, One Billion Rising\n\nFacts:\n- In 1995, Rosario Dawson made her film debut in the teen drama \"Kids.\"\n- In 1999, Rachael Leigh Cook starred in the film \"She's All That.\"\n- In 2001, the film \"Josie and the Pussycats\" depicted a young all-female band that signs with a New York City record label and then discovers the company does not have the musicians' best interests at heart.\n- Rachael Leigh Cook, born on October 4, 1979, is an American actress, model, voice artist, and producer.\n- Rachael Leigh Cook is known for starring in \"Josie and the Pussycats,\" \"Into the West,\" and \"Perception,\" and for voicing characters in \"Robot Chicken\" and Tifa Lockhart in the English version of \"\".\n- In 2013, Studio One Eighty Nine co-founders Rosario Dawson and Abrima Erwiah created Fashion Rising in honor of the V-Day Movement’s One Billion Rising campaign.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
